# Count Triplets with Sum Smaller Than Target

**Pattern:** Sorting + Two Pointers

## Approach
1. Sort the array.
2. Fix the first element using `i`.
3. Initialize `low = i + 1` and `high = n - 1`.
4. Calculate `sum = nums[i] + nums[low] + nums[high]`.
5. If `sum < target`:
   - All elements from `low + 1` to `high` form valid triplets with `nums[i]` and `nums[low]`.
   - Add `high - low` to `count`.
   - Increment `low`.
6. Otherwise, decrement `high`.
7. Return `count`.

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {
    int countTriplets(int target, int nums[]) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int count = 0;

        Arrays.sort(nums);

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {
            int low = i + 1;
            int high = n - 1;

            while (low < high) {
                int sum = nums[i] + nums[low] + nums[high];

                if (sum < target) {
                    count += high - low;
                    low++;
                } else {
                    high--;
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
}
